  "remaining_requirements_note": "The caravan ordering is front member, ego, rear member. \u201cFront gap\u201d is between the front member and ego; \u201crear gap\u201d is between ego and the rear member. Gap values and speeds in the tables are controller requests, not measured constant separations or legal safety cutoffs. Each recording is 30 s; the common schedule includes following, a leader slowdown at 14 s, a restoration request at 19 s, and braking at 22 s.\n\nThe reused no-outsider reference is the accepted 60 m / 6 m/s recording (original job 588), linked directly in Entry front, Entry rear and Group speed. The smaller-entrant reference is the accepted Lincoln front-entry recording (original job 604), linked directly in Entrant dimensions. Reused rows refer to the same video, trace and metadata; they are not additional recordings. Entry front tests outsider presence; Entrant dimensions tests the entering vehicle asset and dimensions. Group speed contains a 6 versus 9 m/s comparison.\n\nCoverage gap: the 30/60/90 m spacing comparison contains no entering outsider, while the front/rear entry recordings use only a 60 m gap target. There is no accepted comparison here holding the entrant, entry maneuver and speed fixed while varying spacing. These recordings therefore do not directly establish how entry safety changes with gap size. \u201cSufficient space\u201d and \u201cwithout danger\u201d remain unresolved; no labels or set coverage dispositions are changed by this documentation correction.",
